Status: DONE
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/114
Milestone: Show the DS and cartridge-loading animation immediately after ROM selection.
Dependencies: None.
Purpose: Leave the cartridge sidebar before slow local ROM identification or
native-core startup, with visible loading feedback on the physical DS LCD.

Tasks:
- [x] Enter DS play view and close cartridge tools before reading the upload.
- [x] Paint an original looping cartridge insertion on the loading LCD.
- [x] Stop loading on native startup, failure or cancellation; respect reduced motion.
- [x] Preserve the current DS session if a replacement ROM is rejected.
- [x] Verify actual upload events, rendered loading, native handoff and recovery.
- [x] Update the guide, ledger, index and verified issue/Project backlink.

Acceptance criteria:
The local upload event reveals DS play view while ROM reading is still pending.
The physical lower LCD animates while reading and booting; reduced motion uses
a static cartridge. Native pixels replace loading on success. Invalid files
surface the established error UI without losing an existing DS session.
Cancel remains usable during native startup. No commercial ROM fixture,
third-party animation, gate bypass, reduced renderer sharpness or frozen-book edit.
Technical completion and monitored publication are recorded separately.

Completion evidence:
